/** \file p4_local.dox
 * \brief User's guide for P4 pixel-local processing.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup p4_local_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * Pixel-local processing evaluates one finite-amplitude trial companion over a bounded sky stamp. It uses the
 * ordinary detector-frame P4 algorithm and the configured retained temporal sample set, but avoids fitting detector
 * pixels that cannot contribute to the requested result. This is the evaluation path used by
 * \ref p4_optimizer_user_guide "negative-planet optimization".
 *
 * \section p4_local_algorithm Exact finite-amplitude refitting
 *
 * Set `p4.localStampSize=W>0` to replace the complete output-field calculation with one local trial. For every
 * detector search pixel needed by the requested sky stamp and every temporal row, the configured perturbation
 * \f$D_t\f$ changes both sides of the regression:
 *
 * \f[
 *   y'_p(t)=I_t(p)+D_t(p), \qquad
 *   X'_p(t,k)=S_{p,k}[I_t]+S_{p,k}[D_t].
 * \f]
 *
 * P4 then repeats its ordinary eigensolve. This is an exact finite-amplitude refit, not the frozen-coefficient PSF
 * response described in the main \ref p4reduce_user_guide "P4 guide". With positive `p4.numberImages`, every
 * selected physical-frame central-pixel sample receives the perturbation before P4 takes the configured temporal
 * mean or median. Every unique detector search pixel is fit once with its complete configured time sequence, while only the residual rows needed by the
 * local derotation footprints are retained. Cubic footprints are unioned over the complete field rotation, so the
 * number of fitted detector pixels is generally greater than `W*W` but much smaller than a complete output field.
 * When `adi.excludeMethod` is non-`none`, every requested target residual is calculated from its own retained-row
 * fit through the configured `solver.exclusionSolver` and `solver.deletionBackend`. Per-target rank support is propagated into
 * the sparse local validity product. For an evaluation using an explicit frame subset, including a jackknife refit,
 * `imno` distances index that ordered retained subset rather than the original pre-subset cube.
 *
 * The source center is never quantized. Full images and the source template use the geometric center
 * `0.5*(N-1)` in each axis. For final-sky separation \f$r\f$ and position angle \f$\theta\f$, the continuous source
 * coordinate is
 *
 * \f[
 *   x_s = \frac{1}{2}(N_x-1)-r\sin\theta, \qquad
 *   y_s = \frac{1}{2}(N_y-1)+r\cos\theta.
 * \f]
 *
 * The odd result lattice is anchored at `floor(source+0.5)` in each axis, but the template remains centered on the
 * continuous coordinate. Its internal crop is the smallest dimension at least `localStampSize` with the same parity
 * as the detector and source template. Thus an 11-pixel result on an even-sized detector uses a centered 12-pixel
 * template crop instead of shifting the half-pixel center. Detector and template parity must match.
 *
 * \section p4_local_configuration Configuration
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | FITS keyword | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--p4.localStampSize` | `p4.localStampSize=11` | `HIERARCH P4 LOCAL STAMP SIZE` | zero or positive odd integer | `0` | Return this square sky stamp after one finite-amplitude local refit. Zero preserves complete-field P4 processing. |
 *
 * The trial uses `fake.fileName`, `fake.sep`, `fake.PA`, `fake.contrast`, and optional `fake.scaleFileName` from the
 * shared \ref common_configuration_dictionary "configuration dictionary". Exactly one separation, position angle,
 * and finite contrast must be supplied, and `fake.method=single` is required.
 * When `fake.subtractPlanet=true`, each configured `[planet]` tuple is also sampled at negative contrast during every
 * local evaluation. This fixed subtraction is not added to the fake vectors and is not an optimizer parameter.
 *
 * The current local contract requires:
 *
 * - `preProcess.skip=true` and a template representing the already-preprocessed P4 input stage;
 * - detector-frame P4, enabled derotation, and a final `combine.method`;
 * - `adi.postMedSub=false` and `output.outputPSFSub=false`;
 * - `p4.numberImages=0` when target-frame exclusion is enabled; and
 * - no frozen-model settings (`p4.psfFile`, `p4.outputPSFModels`, or `p4.psfFilter`).
 *
 * The gap-held-out `p4.temporalPredictor=pcat` mode is not yet available for pixel-local trials because the temporal
 * basis would need to be re-fit after every trial perturbation.
 *
 * Inherited fake injection is inactive when preprocessing is skipped. Pixel-local P4 samples the trial on demand, so
 * the loaded input cube remains pristine and trial flux does not accumulate across repeated evaluations.
 *
 * For example, evaluate one 11-pixel negative trial against already-preprocessed input:
 *
 * \code{.sh}
 * p4Reduce -c prepared-p4.conf \
 *   --preProcess.skip=true \
 *   --p4.localStampSize=11 \
 *   --fake.method=single \
 *   --fake.fileName=/path/post-preprocess-psf.fits \
 *   --fake.sep=13 --fake.PA=100 --fake.contrast=-0.001
 * \endcode
 *
 * \section p4_local_products Products and provenance
 *
 * The standard final-image product becomes a `localStampSize x localStampSize x modeCount` cube with
 * `HIERARCH P4 PRODUCT ROLE=LOCAL_RESIDUAL`. An exact zero/one validity cube inserts `local_validity` before the
 * normal sequence number and is stored in the residual's auxiliary directory. For example, `finim_0000.fits` uses
 * `finim_0000_outputs/finim_local_validity_0000.fits`. With an exact filename it becomes
 * `<stem>_outputs/<stem>_local_validity<extension>`.
 *
 * Both products record the integer full-image origin, continuous source coordinate, center and lattice conventions,
 * actual template-crop dimensions, unique detector-fit count, sparse residual-sample count, fake-source provenance,
 * and `POST_PREPROCESS_P4_INPUT` injection stage. The memory policy includes the retained sparse dependency map and
 * records its exact dynamic allocation as `HIERARCH P4 LOCAL GEOMETRY BYTES`.
 *
 * @}
 */
